# oxi-adapter-{{ADAPTER_SLUG}} — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values you actually use. The `.env` next
# to this file is gitignored by oxi's default .gitignore. Tools that read
# .env (direnv, dotenv) will load these automatically; in a plain shell:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# OXI_ADAPTER is already written to `.env` by `oxi init`; the keys below
# are optional and only matter for the non-agentic InferenceGateway path
# (planner heuristics, classification, ranking, dedup, summary). The
# agentic worker (`claude -p`) uses your Anthropic CLI credentials and
# is unaffected by anything here.
#
# See https://github.com/escotilha/oxibyoxi/blob/main/docs/runbooks/litellm-gateway.md
# for the full story on routing roles to providers.

# --- Anthropic (default for every non-agentic role) ---
# Used both by the agentic `claude -p` worker AND the non-agentic
# InferenceGateway. If you only have this one key, you're done.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- OpenRouter (optional, via LiteLLM gateway) ---
# Lets you route cheap heuristics (e.g. classification, dedup) to
# OpenRouter-hosted models. Requires a LiteLLM gateway provisioned
# with the upstream OPENROUTER_API_KEY; the value below is the
# *virtual key* the gateway issues to oxi.
# LITELLM_VIRTUAL_KEY_OPENROUTER=sk-...

# --- xAI / Grok (optional, via LiteLLM gateway) ---
# Same pattern: virtual key issued by your LiteLLM gateway, which
# itself holds the upstream XAI_API_KEY.
# LITELLM_VIRTUAL_KEY_XAI=sk-...

# --- LiteLLM gateway URL (optional, defaults to local) ---
# OXI_INFERENCE_GATEWAY_URL=http://mac-mini.tail-net.ts.net:4000
